  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The symbol \\(|a|\\) means \\(+a\\) if \\(a\\) is greater than or equal to zero, and \\(-a\\) if \\(a\\) is less than or equal to zero; the symbol \\(\\lt\\) means “less than”; the symbol \\(\\gt\\) means “greater than.” The set of values \\(x\\) satisfying the inequality \\(|3-x|\\lt4\\) consists of all \\(x\\) such that:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x^2\\lt49\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x^2\\gt1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\lt x^2\\lt49\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-1\\lt x\\lt7\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-7\\lt x\\lt1\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1959-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The absolute-value inequality is equivalent to \\[ -4\\lt3-x\\lt4. \\] Subtracting \\(3\\) and multiplying by \\(-1\\) reverses the inequalities, giving \\[ -1\\lt x\\lt7. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(|3-x|\\lt4\\) as a compound inequality",
        "Solve \\(-4\\lt3-x\\lt4\\) for \\(x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
